  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 109 PM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nWednesday through the end of the work week, weak low pressure will \nbe located across Texas, with upper level ridging well to our east \nacross the Atlantic. Despite the lower heights across the region, \ndry and warm conditions are forecast to prevail. Highs will be in \nthe mid 80s to lower 90s. Overnight low will generally be in the \n60s. An isolated shower or thunderstorm is possible Friday, but\nexpect most locations to remain dry. Weak upper level ridging is \nthen forecast to develop this late this weekend into early next \nweek. This will result in temperatures a degree or two hotter than\nforecast temperatures during the work week, but any impacts will \nbe minimal. Highs will be in the mid 80s to mid 90s. The potential\ntropical disturbance in the Gulf is forecast to track northeast \ntoward the north-central or northeast Gulf and will have no \nimpact on the weather across West Central Texas.",
